  "description": "ORABOC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H72 Er4 N14 O24 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),2(C3 H7 N1 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.635-4.150 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.31-128.44°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H86Er4N18O32.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
